course: dictionary
lesson: 13175
title: Frantic: worried or rushing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Frantic is a word with two meanings. Both come from a mind or body that is moving too fast to be calm. Read the words around it to find out which one the author means. «Mum was frantic when she could not find my little brother.» The clue is the worry, so frantic means very worried, so that she could not think clearly.
explain: The second meaning is about action. «Dad made a frantic search for his keys before the school bus came.» Searching is an action, and the bus is a deadline, so frantic means done very quickly and wildly, with lots of rushing.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If you swap in "very worried" or "wild and rushing" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Frantic is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a parent, a search or a rush.
fact: Frantic means very worried, scared or upset, so that you cannot think calmly.
fact: Frantic also means done very quickly and wildly, with lots of rushing.
fact: Common phrases: «frantic with worry», «a frantic search», «a frantic rush».
fact: Frantic is an adjective: frantic, more frantic, most frantic.
fact: In safety lessons, staying calm is better than being frantic.
exercise: «Mum was frantic when she could not find my little brother.» What does frantic mean here? | *Very worried, so she could not think calmly | Very happy about the holiday | Very calm and relaxed | Very tired and sleepy
exercise: «Dad made a frantic search for his keys.» What kind of search was it? | *Quick, wild and rushing | Slow and calm | Quiet and gentle | Long and boring
exercise: In a fire drill, what is better: to stay calm or to be frantic? | Run in circles | Be frantic | Shout at everyone | *Stay calm
test: «He was frantic with worry when his dog ran off.» What feeling does this show? | *Very worried and upset | Happy and proud | Calm and relaxed | Bored and sleepy
test: «The frantic bees buzzed around the flowers as the storm came.» What does frantic mean here? | Very quiet | *Rushing wildly | Sleeping | Very clean
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to frantic when someone is rushing wildly? | Calm | *Hasty | Gentle | Slow
